    <string name="info_prepare">Countdown before the first set, so you have time to get into position. Set to 0 to skip it.</string>

    <string name="info_sets">The number of work sets in the workout. Each set is followed by a rest except the last one.</string>

    <string name="info_work">How long each work set lasts. For Counter workouts, the rep table shows how many reps to do in each set.</string>

    <string name="info_rest">The break between sets. There is no rest after the final set.</string>

    <string name="info_cooldown">Countdown after the last set. Set to 0 to skip it.</string>

    <string name="info_total">The total workout time, including preparation, work, rests and cooldown. Maximum 2 hours.</string>

    <string name="info_starting_total">The number of reps in your first workout, and after you reset your progress. It must be between your minimum and maximum.</string>

    <string name="info_floor">The lowest your rep total can go, no matter how long you are away.</string>

    <string name="info_cap">The highest your rep total can go. Once you reach it, on-time check-ins keep you at the same number.</string>

    <string name="info_hold">Want to stay at a certain number for a while? A hold lets you pause your progression. For example, you could hold at 80 reps for several check-ins before climbing again. You can set multiple holds.</string>

    <string name="info_hold_at">The rep total where progression pauses. It must be at or above your minimum and below your maximum.</string>

    <string name="info_hold_for">How many check-ins to stay at this number before increasing again. The check-in that first reaches it counts. Set to 0 to skip the hold.</string>

    <string name="info_window">Check in within this many hours of your last check-in to stay on time. On-time check-ins continue your streak and, for Counter workouts, add one rep.</string>

    <string name="info_penalty_rate">After you miss the on-time window, your rep total gradually decreases while you are away. The total never falls below your minimum.</string>

    <string name="info_total_reps">Your current rep total, divided across the workout\'s sets. Changes take effect immediately.</string>

    <string name="info_best_streak">Your longest run of on-time check-ins. It updates on its own as your streak grows.</string>

    <string name="info_current_streak">Your current run of on-time check-ins, including the latest one. Missing the window resets the streak to 1.</string>

    <string name="info_last_check_in">The last time you pressed Start. REPKIT uses this to calculate your on-time window and missed-day adjustment. Clear it to make your next check-in the first one.</string>

    <string name="info_sound">Plays countdown beeps and a beep whenever the workout changes phase.</string>

    <string name="info_vibration">Vibrates whenever the workout changes phase, even when the screen is off.</string>

